' =====================================================================
' New: lock primitive + sweeper
' =====================================================================

class MonitorLockRepository <<NEW>> {
  + try_acquire(key, instance_id) : bool
  + refresh(key, instance_id) : bool
  + release(key, instance_id) : void
  - _LOCK_TTL_SEC : int = 60
  - _REFRESH_LUA : str
}
note right of MonitorLockRepository
  **NEW**.  Single-purpose wrapper around the
  Redis lock primitive used by all three monitor
  flows.

  ``try_acquire``  — SET key {instance_id} NX EX 60.
                      Returns True if won.
  ``refresh``      — Lua: GET key == instance_id then
                      EXPIRE key 60.  Returns False if
                      another instance owns it now (or
                      key is gone).  Caller self-terminates.
  ``release``      — Lua: GET key == instance_id then
                      DEL key.  Best-effort; lock would
                      expire on its own anyway.

  Lua refresh + release is the only correct shape:
  plain EXPIRE / DEL would clobber another instance's
  lock if Redis hiccupped and ownership shifted.
end note

class MonitorLockSweeper <<NEW>> {
  + start() : void
  + stop() : void
  - _tick() : void
  - _sweep_per_job(fleet) : void
  - _sweep_community() : void
  - _interval_sec : int = 30
  - _instance_id : str
}
note right of MonitorLockSweeper
  **NEW**.  Single thread per instance, no
  leader gating.  Started at boot on every
  Cloud Run instance.

  **Per tick** (every 30s):
   1. SELECT id FROM jobs WHERE
        status='running' AND
        machine_type IN ('vast_serverless',
                         'modal_serverless')
   2. For each row, try_acquire
        ``monitor:job:{job_id}``.
        Win → call the corresponding callback
        handler's ``start_monitoring(...)``
        which spawns the per-job thread on
        THIS instance.
        Lose → another instance owns it. Skip.
   3. try_acquire ``monitor:community``.
        Win → call ``CommunityMonitor.try_start()``.
        Lose → skip.

  Stateless across runs.  All authoritative state
  lives in the DB row + Redis lock.
end note

MonitorLockSweeper --> MonitorLockRepository : try_acquire

