class VastCallbackHandler <<CHANGED>> {
  + start_monitoring(...) : void
  + stop_monitoring(job_id) : void
  - _monitors : dict
}
note right of VastCallbackHandler
  **CHANGED**: ``start_monitoring`` first
  calls ``MonitorLockRepository.try_acquire(
    f"monitor:job:{job_id}", instance_id)``.
  Spawns the thread only on win.

  Two callers now:
   1. ``VastFleetStrategy.dispatch`` (at dispatch
      time, on the dispatching instance).
   2. ``MonitorLockSweeper._sweep_per_job``
      (at sweep time, on whichever instance's
      tick fires first for an unowned job).

  Both go through the same lock acquire — at
  most one wins per ``job_id``.

  Local ``_monitors`` dict still de-dups within
  a single instance; the Redis lock is the
  cross-instance dedup.
end note

