class CommunityMonitor <<CHANGED>> {
  + try_start() : bool
  + stop() : void
  - _loop() : void
  - _tick() : void
}
note right of CommunityMonitor
  **CHANGED**:
   * New ``try_start()`` returns True iff
     ``MonitorLockRepository.try_acquire(
       "monitor:community", instance_id)``
     succeeds; spawns the thread on win.
     If a sweeper later finds the lock free
     (this instance died), another instance's
     sweeper calls ``try_start()`` and gets
     the win.
   * On every tick (~10s) the loop calls
     ``MonitorLockRepository.refresh(...)``;
     if it returns False the loop exits
     (lost ownership; another instance has
     taken over via the sweeper).
end note

