' =====================================================================
' Boot wiring
' =====================================================================

class "main.py (FastAPI startup hook)" as main_py <<CHANGED>>
note right of main_py
  **CHANGED** (lines 71-77):

  Today:
    if try_acquire_leader_lock():
        _run_recovery(_container)
        _drain_queues_after_recovery(_container)
        _container.community_monitor.start()

  After:
    _container.community_monitor.try_start()
    _container.monitor_lock_sweeper.start()
    _drain_queues_after_recovery(_container)

  Leader election goes away entirely (advisory-lock
  helper + the if/else branch + the leader-only
  daemon startup path).  Every instance runs the
  same boot sequence.

  ``community_monitor.try_start()`` is the fast
  path -- on the first booted instance it gets
  the lock and starts immediately, before the
  sweeper's first tick lands.

  ``MonitorLockSweeper`` covers everything from
  there on: claims orphans (community, vast jobs,
  modal jobs) within sweep_interval + lock_TTL
  worst case after the previous owner died.
end note

main_py ..> CommunityMonitor : try_start
main_py ..> MonitorLockSweeper : start

